<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Church of the Holy Spirit, Heidelberg</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Heiliggeistkirche Heidelberg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Church of the Holy Spirit is the main church of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg">Heidelberg</a>'s old town, built in Gothic style from 1398 and the burial place of several <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> palatine. Its galleries once housed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bibliotheca-palatina">Bibliotheca Palatina</a>. From 1706 it was divided by a wall between Catholics and Protestants, and a dispute over its use in 1719–1720 led Elector Charles III Philip to move his residence to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mannheim">Mannheim</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/church-of-the-holy-spirit-heidelberg.jpg" alt="Church of the Holy Spirit, Heidelberg" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Hlohning assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heidelberg_20060420_021.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
